/** \page imgui-hooks ImGui Hooks

Sometimes features need to be added into the ImGui source code. This can be performed with the ImGui hooks system; a
CMake module to dynamically add function hooks at configure-time.

All files to do with the module are in the `cmake/ImGuiHooks` directory.

Due to the module being run at configure-time, changes will only take place on a CMake reload.

\section callbacks Callbacks

The callback is the function call added by the hook. It contains all parameters of the hooked function, with the first
being the class instance if the `add_this` property is true, and the function is a member function.

The callback function returns a boolean; true indicating the original function should return there, or false to resume
execution of the original function.

\section imgui-hooks-json imgui_hooks.json

The `imgui_hooks.json` file lists the function hooks that need to be installed, and their related callback functions.

<table>
<tr>
<th>Property</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`file`</td>
<td>The source file to modify.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`function`</td>
<td>The ImGui function name to module. Must contain the fully-qualified name if in a class.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`include_file`</td>
<td>The header file to include (where the callback function is declared).</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`callback`</td>
<td>The callback function to add to the hook.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`add_this`</td>
<td>Whether to add the `this` parameter to the callback function. Only applicable to member functions.</td>
</tr>
</table>

*/
